 "about": "Living people the Flagships tab never names: in prose, in a source's title or in a source's address (codex58). A house keeps its name, so an entry that is also the name of the record's own producer (Egon Müller, Franz Hirtzberger, Álvaro Palacios) is not refused there, and an entry inside the producer's full name as the record writes it (Domaine Jean-Louis Chave) is not refused either; anywhere else the person is said as the family, the founder's great grandson, the cellar master. Each name is matched folded (no accents, no case) as whole words. The list grows as checkers find names: add the person's name as a writer would print it, and the surname alone only where it names nobody else in the wave. The long dead are named with their dates and are never listed here. The critics and writers of .scripts/grapes/schema.cjs (LIVING) are refused as well.",
